export anchor GlassHubStyle:
    number: 374
    screen: SmartHome
    name: Glass hub
    idea: Every room is a frosted dark glass tile floating over slow coloured light, and a room that is doing something glows softly in its own colour while idle rooms stay clear and still.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #0b0d17, page ground under the light blobs
        glass: #ffffff11, every tile, the top bar and swatch cards
        edge: #ffffff29, 1px tile edges, 30% on buttons and fields
        ink: #eef0fb, text and figures
        mute: #aab0cc, labels, meta and axis text
        warm: #ffcf7a, lights on glow, the alert and evening bars
        mint: #7ff0c8, locked and battery
        lilac: #c9b6ff, motion glow, the active scene and focus halo
        rose: #ffb0a8, heating schedule glow
        sky: #9fd4ff, daytime chart bars
        onWarm: #2a1a00, text on the warm primary button
    type:
        One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. Base 15px at 1.5. Big numbers are thin, the kWh figure 44px
        and room temperatures 40px at weight 250 with the degree sign at
        18px muted. Tile titles 15px at 600, state lines 14px muted, tags
        12px at 650 in caps with 0.04em tracking.
    layout:
        The page ground is near black indigo with three large dim radial
        light blobs, violet top left, teal right and amber bottom, clipped
        by the stage. A full pill glass top bar holds a round B mark, the
        name, Saturday and the time, and a moon line saying Movie scene on.
        Below it a full width glass alert glows amber with a warning bubble,
        the sentence and a cream to amber pill Close now button. A 12 column
        grid follows. The left 8 columns hold five glass room tiles three
        across, each with a round glass icon bubble, a pill state tag top
        right, the room name, a huge thin temperature or a state word, and a
        state line with its own icon. A tile that is doing something glows
        in its colour, amber for lights on, rose for the heating schedule,
        lilac for garden motion, while kitchen and the locked door stay
        clear. The right 4 columns stack Energy today with a thin 44px
        figure, two inner glass chips for solar and battery and a bar chart
        whose evening bars are amber, then Scenes as four tall glass keys
        with Movie lit lilac and marked Active with a check. Below 1060px
        the side column drops under the rooms in two columns, below 760px
        rooms go two across and at phone width one across with scenes two by
        two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between tiles, 18 to 20px tile padding, 32px page gutter and 16px on phones.
    density: Airy. Five room tiles, energy and scenes fill one wide screen.
    corners: 22px tiles, full pills for the top bar, tags and buttons, 18px scene keys and round icon bubbles.
    borders:
        1px white at 16 percent on every glass surface, a tinted edge at
        about 50 percent on a glowing tile, 30 percent white on buttons and
        fields.
    shadows:
        An inset 1px white top highlight and 0 12px 32px black at 35 percent
        on glass. Active tiles add a 36px coloured glow, and the alert a
        40px amber glow.
    icons:
        Round line icons at 1.6 stroke, 20px, in 44px glass bubbles. States
        use a bulb for on, a dash circle for off, a flame for the schedule,
        a check for locked and a walking figure for motion, always beside a
        word.
    focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px with a 6px lilac halo, visible on glass and on glow.
    tone: Short and calm, such as Energy today, Scenes, Active and Close now.
